target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckRefusesAnUnreadableRecord'
verify: go test ./cmd/looper/ -count=1 -run 'TestPrReportRefusesARunItCannotRead'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    RETARGETED with its sibling. The emptiness must be DERIVED from what the load produced, never asserted: hardcoding it false restores the state where misresolving a store — a wrong -store, a missing file, a mistyped -run-id — is the cheapest way to make both halves of the gate say yes, and record.Load returns an empty map with NO error for every one of those. Distinct from the keys-on-the-map entry beside it: that one tests a predicate too narrow to see a row that says nothing, this one tests a predicate that is not a predicate.
--- old
func (r *Run) Empty() bool {
	return r == nil || (r.Plan == nil && len(r.Cycles) == 0 && r.Finish == nil)
}
--- new
func (r *Run) Empty() bool {
	return false
}
